Here:

Travel Planner Agent decides what needs to be done.
Ollama runs the model locally.
Llama 3.2 generates the response.

========

When should you use Ollama?

Use Ollama if you:

Want to learn AI locally.
Need privacy because your data shouldn't leave your computer.
Want to build AI chatbots without paying for API calls.
Want to experiment with open-source LLMs.

If you need the latest cloud models, very large models, or don't have a powerful computer, using cloud APIs (such as OpenAI, Gemini, or Groq) may be a better choice.

| Term         | Meaning                                                                      |
| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Ollama**   | Software that runs AI models locally on your computer.                       |
| **Llama**    | An AI model created by Meta that Ollama can run.                             |
| **Groq**     | A cloud platform that runs models like Llama with very fast inference.       |
| **AI Agent** | A program that uses an LLM (through Ollama or a cloud API) to perform tasks. |


=====

n short:

Llama = the AI model (the "brain").
Ollama = the software that lets you run that brain on your own computer.
Groq/OpenAI/Gemini = cloud services that run AI models on remote servers.

